+"""v7.0.96: a Resume that cannot progress must escalate once, not repeat the same wait forever.
+
+Field case (job 20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729, shot_023_open.jpg): the saved journal named
+project ca1709fe-..., but Flow was showing another project (the request had been submitted in a project the
+job never recorded). Every Resume therefore reopened the wrong project, `capture()` refused with "Image
+project changed", the three attempts ended as "Image recovery checkpoint retained", the journal stayed
+unresolved, and Resume reported "Saved request unresolved; no new generation started" again and again.
+
+The old guidance made it worse: it told the user to archive the request with --confirm-new-credit-spend,
+but image requests are free (config/flow_models.yaml: credits_per_image 0), and every archive increased the
+automatic fresh-request count that generate() uses as a hard stop, so the documented command led to a dead end.
+
+Tested here with fakes only: no browser, no Flow request, no credits.
+"""
+import json
+from pathlib import Path
